# Mini-app standards

- Vite + React + TypeScript with `strict: true` and `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true`. Package manager: `pnpm`; commit the lockfile.
- Linter/formatter: Biome. Tests: Vitest + Testing Library.
- API types and client are generated from the backend OpenAPI schema. Never hand-write API types or duplicate backend contracts.
- Server state via TanStack Query. No global mutable singletons.
- Telegram integration only through the official community SDK chosen in the bootstrap prompt; `initData` is sent to the backend unmodified and never trusted client-side.
- Do not store personal data, rule text or contact labels in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, `DeviceStorage` or cookies. UI preferences only.
- No third-party analytics, fonts, CDNs or trackers. Assets are bundled; Content-Security-Policy must remain strict.
- All user-facing strings go through the localization catalog.
- Accessibility: semantic elements, labelled controls, respects Telegram theme parameters.
